---
// Site-specific privacy information. The statements about cookies, tracking
// and third-party requests stay true as long as no analytics, embeds or
// externally hosted assets are added.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy information for the website of the DFG Research Unit KI-FOR 5339.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This website is operated by the Karlsruhe Institute of Technology. The
        <a href="https://www.kit.edu/privacypolicy.php">privacy policy of KIT</a> applies. This page summarises what the
        website itself does and how it is hosted.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>No cookies, no tracking</h2>
      <p>
        The website sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking. It loads no content from third parties. Fonts,
        images and scripts are delivered from this website itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The website is hosted on GitHub Pages by GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St., San Francisco, CA 94107,
        United States. When you open a page, GitHub records in log files the data that your browser sends: your IP
        address, the address of the page you came from, the date and time of the request, the page requested, the HTTP
        status code, the amount of data transferred, and information about your browser and operating system.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is necessary to display the website and to keep it stable and secure, which is our legitimate interest
        under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. It is not required by law or contract, but the website cannot work without it. There
        is no tracking, and we have no direct access to these data. GitHub receives them as a recipient of your
        personal data, and its servers are in the United States. For transfers of personal data from the EU, GitHub
        relies on the standard contractual clauses of the European Commission. Further information, including how to
        object, is given in the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub
        privacy statement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You have the right to object to this processing; whether an objection succeeds depends on a weighing of
        interests. The data are deleted as soon as they are no longer needed for this purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to publishers, institutes and other external websites take you to services that are not operated by KIT.
        Their own privacy policies apply there.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about data protection, please contact the Data Protection Officer of KIT at
        <a href="mailto:datenschutzbeauftragte@kit.edu">datenschutzbeauftragte@kit.edu</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
